  "known_limitations": [
    "Actual spreadsheet-selected native implementation is Rust, not C/C++; Python drives it through existing C ABI. No rewritten algorithm is claimed.",
    "Local lzbench has LZSSE2/4/8, not the specified Okumura EI10/EJ4 LZSS. Analysis document coverage claim is corrected by source review; source exception is explicit.",
    "Original library EOF tolerance is insufficient: project independently rejects truncated tokens, surplus bytes and nonzero padding. No checksum means arbitrary structurally valid payload changes cannot be detected without common correctness.",
    "Fixed benchmark parameters EI10/EJ4/C32, stack work buffers, safe/std/alloc features, one thread, one stream per routed object; streaming/query/random access and alternative parameters are unregistered.",
    "Rust sanitizer uses pinned host stable rustc with RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1 and -Zsanitizer=address; codec and FFI are instrumented, prebuilt std is not. C++ ABI is ASan/UBSan; LSan disabled due host ptrace policy.",
    "void 1.0.2 archive matches original Cargo.lock SHA256 and declares MIT in Cargo.toml/README but contains no license text. Local execution allowed; redistribution requires license review.",
    "Criterion benchmark source informs parameters/API, but Criterion timing and best-time summaries are not imported. Offline rustc runs actual original sources/build generator/tests without fetching Criterion.",
    "block_size is a framework boundary fixture parameter, not a second LZSS window or an implicit segmentation stage."
  ],
